Falsifies `byte_glob::verification::a_negated_class_is_the_exact_complement_of_the_class`.

The defect: `class_at` consumes the `!` of `[!...]` but never applies the negation, so `[!ab]` matches exactly
what `[ab]` matches.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(matches_with(&plain, ..), !matches_with(&negated, ..))`.

diff --git a/crates/byte_glob/src/lib.rs b/crates/byte_glob/src/lib.rs
index 661ecd445..26af48ba9 100644
--- a/crates/byte_glob/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/byte_glob/src/lib.rs
@@ -490,3 +490,3 @@ fn class_at(pattern: &[u8], open: usize, c: u8) -> (Option<(bool, usize)>, usize
         if byte == b']' && !at_start {
-            return (Some((hit ^ negated, k + 1)), scanned);
+            return (Some((hit, k + 1)), scanned);
         }
